  If you were human sacrificing a human corpse a) converts the 
altar to chaotic 100% guaranteed (if it wasn't already) and b) 
summons a peaceful major demon.  Unfortunately they're human
and you're not, so same-race sacrifice rules don't apply.
(Note that your sacrificing a corpse from an elven mummy/zombie
counts as same-race sacrifice and bypasses any checks for the
age of the corpse.)

  The first two peaceful major demons summoned this way are 
Yeenoghu and Juiblex.  Meaning you won't see Juiblex hostile 
later on his level.  He and Yeenoghu will be a deity-damned pain 
teleporting into your way until you lead them up or down stairs.

  After they show up you'll start summoning "regular" peaceful 
major demons, some of which will be foocubi.  An unscrupulous
wizard might take advantage of these unsuspecting foocubi.
(Note that since they will be peaceful, you will have to initiate
any encounters with the #chat command.  Making them hostile is 
left as an exercise for the reader.)

  This is the reason I play chaotic *human* wizards, as Fort 
Ludious provides a large number of humans to carry their 
equipment to the nearest altar, and then be sacrificed on it.


